From 93e4ae45cfc114deb727cacc18c660ab7737d924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: Japanese voices from the player's Japanese disc;
 the room checks everyone's mods

Mods & expansions gets a JAPANESE VOICES section: the player chooses their Japanese disc (Sonic
Riders, Japan, GXEJ8P; any image the launcher reads), and the launcher makes the file mod
srnp_voix_jp in their Mods folder and turns it on: the files only the US disc has (voices in the
race, menus, Chao, story cutscenes, films, tutorial), each served from its Japanese counterpart
under the English name; one identical to the English file is left out (launcher_voices.cpp, as
tools/srnp's construire_mod_voix_jp.py does). Nothing of the game is in the code: the files come
from the player's disc. --japanese-voices <disc image> does the same without the window.

Online/LAN play: the room's protocol SRNP-ONLINE-2 adds each player's fingerprint of the file mods
the match's game loads (name, mod.ini, files and sizes); START needs the host's mods for everyone
("OTHER MODS" otherwise): a mod's files do not load at the disc's pace (measured with the Japanese
voices: ~414 frames ahead on a cold start), so the games would leave lockstep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
